    "text": "To find the length of the paint trail left by the tennis ball, we need to determine the arc length of the parametric curve given by \\((x(t), y(t)) = (3t^2 - 9t - 5, t^2 - 3t + 2)\\) for \\(0 \\le t \\le 4\\). The formula for the arc length \\(L\\) of a parametric curve \\((x(t), y(t))\\) from \\(t = a\\) to \\(t = b\\) is:\n\n\\[\nL = \\int_a^b \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to find the derivatives \\(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\) and \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\nx(t) = 3t^2 - 9t - 5\n\\]\n\\[\ny(t) = t^2 - 3t + 2\n\\]\n\nCompute \\(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(3t^2 - 9t - 5) = 6t - 9\n\\]\n\nCompute \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(t^2 - 3t + 2) = 2t - 3\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\) and \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\) into the arc length formula:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{(6t - 9)^2 + (2t - 3)^2} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression inside the square root:\n\\[\n(6t - 9)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81\n\\]\n\\[\n(2t - 3)^2 = 4t^2 - 12t + 9\n\\]\n\\[\n(6t - 9)^2 + (2t - 3)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81 + 4t^2 - 12t + 9 = 40t^2 - 120t + 90\n\\]\n\nThus, the arc length integral becomes:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{40t^2 - 120t + 90} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nFactor out the constant from the square root:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{40(t^2 - 3t + \\frac{9}{4}) + 40 \\cdot \\frac{9}{4} - 40 \\cdot \\frac{9}{4}} \\, dt = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{40(t^2 - 3t + \\frac{9}{4})} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression inside the square root:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{40} \\sqrt{t^2 - 3t + \\frac{9}{4}} \\, dt = \\sqrt{40} \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{t^2 - 3t + \\frac{9}{4}} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nComplete the square for the quadratic expression inside the square root:\n\\[\nt^2 - 3t + \\frac{9}{4} = \\left(t - \\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2\n\\]\n\nThus, the integral becomes:\n\\[\nL = \\sqrt{40} \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{\\left(t - \\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2} \\, dt = \\sqrt{40} \\int_0^4 \\left| t - \\frac{3}{2} \\right| \\, dt\n\\]\n\nSince \\(0 \\le t \\le 4\\), we have \\(t - \\frac{3}{2} \\ge 0\\), so \\(\\left| t - \\frac{3}{2} \\right| = t - \\frac{3}{2}\\):\n\\[\nL = \\sqrt{40} \\int_0^4 \\left( t - \\frac{3}{2} \\right) \\, dt\n\\]\n\nEvaluate the integral:\n\\[\n\\int_0^4 \\left( t - \\frac{3}{2} \\right) \\, dt = \\left[ \\frac{t^2}{2} - \\frac{3t}{2} \\right]_0",
